      "value": "@{5e59bc346312bf2d549f33ab|full_name} What makes you believe the Unity 2022 version used by VRChat is unsafe?\n\nIf you've found an exploitable security vulnerability, you can resport it responsibly at https://help.vrchat.com/hc/en-us/requests/new with proof-of-concepts, documentation, attack scenarios, potential mitigations, etc.\n\nSwitching to Unity 6 is also technically challenging with years of user-generated content in VRChat built on previous rendering pipelines, and switching to Unity 6's SRP/URP from Unity 2022's BIRP would potentially break lots of avatars and worlds. (Preserving the [Treehouse in the Shade](https://vrchat.com/home/launch?worldId=wrld_551c30cb-0e56-4c69-9176-10e259a89e2a) in memoriam of 1001 could be a challenge, for example.)\n\nThis is also a duplicate feature request of: https://feedback.vrchat.com/feature-requests/p/inevitable-vrc-upgrades-to-unity-6-lts",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
